WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.822
Alumni keep the scoreboard forever.

00:00:01.822 --> 00:00:04.374
The course ends; the loop does not.

00:00:04.374 --> 00:00:06.561
This lesson is about alumni loop.

00:00:06.561 --> 00:00:07.654
Keep scoreboard forever.

00:00:07.654 --> 00:00:10.205
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:10.205 --> 00:00:13.850
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:19.317
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:19.317 --> 00:00:23.327
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:23.327 --> 00:00:27.336
Stay practical: schedule monthly review before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:27.656 --> 00:00:31.355
Schedule a monthly review: money, conversations, delivery, next experiment.

00:00:31.355 --> 00:00:33.821
Remember the objective: schedule monthly review.

00:00:33.821 --> 00:00:38.342
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:38.342 --> 00:00:43.274
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:43.274 --> 00:00:47.795
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:47.795 --> 00:00:52.727
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:52.727 --> 00:00:55.604
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:55.604 --> 00:00:57.248
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:00:57.568 --> 00:00:59.108
Keep the weekly OS.

